{"ts":"2026-07-14T11:18:18.021Z","type":"quest-declared","sealed":{"doneWhen":{"probe":"scenario-harness","args":{"scenario":"service-install-catalog-owner","reportDir":"test-output/reports/service-install-catalog-owner","consecutive":3,"metric":"priority"}},"frontierMetrics":[{"probe":"scenario-harness","args":{"scenario":"service-install-catalog-owner","reportDir":"test-output/reports/service-install-catalog-owner","metric":"priority"}}],"authoringContractVersion":1,"statement":"The cluster service install catalog deterministically serializes overlapping intent, classifies cross-owner insert conflicts through authoritative replay, applies rollout and latest-failure updates with a single-winner durable fence, treats stale failure replay as a no-op, completes partial failure attachment exactly once, and still records unsupported activation as recorded_not_running without owning runtime actual state.","class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."},{"id":"sealed-owner-scope","statement":"The bounded replacement covers the existing service install catalog constants, four bootstrap schemas, explicit CDC policies, production owner contract and factory wiring, scenario runner, and production-factory test. Architecture prose is aligned separately after terminal handoff."},{"id":"concurrent-create-contract","statement":"Overlapping resource identities are registered synchronously before any await. Durable primary and operation uniqueness is the cross-owner backstop: late success or duplicate insert is authoritatively re-read and returns either the unchanged projection or a closed typed conflict."},{"id":"single-winner-update-contract","statement":"Rollout and latest-failure updates use the observed rollout state plus a strictly monotonic updated_at value as a durable compare-and-swap fence. Incompatible concurrent updates produce exactly one durable winner; a stale writer cannot overwrite it."},{"id":"failure-replay-contract","statement":"An already-durable failure replay is a no-op whenever any latest_failure_id is present. An immutable failure left by a partial write may attach exactly once only while that pointer is null."},{"id":"parent-invariants-preserved","statement":"Package and revision identities remain immutable, initial activation remains recorded_not_running, caller actual-state fields fail closed, corrupt running state is never projected, and services plus service_endpoints retain actual-state ownership."},{"id":"negative-attacks","statement":"Deterministic two-owner barriers must prove identical install replay, typed identity conflicts, one-winner rollout and failure races, stale losing-failure no-op, partial failure completion, and lost insert/update response recovery. Independent verification must also re-run the recorded_not_running, package immutability, and actual-state guard revert mutants."},{"id":"downstream-exclusions","statement":"This Quest does not add lifecycle SQL, artifact fetching, reconciliation scheduling, runtime activation, endpoint publication, registry access, or CLI commands."}],"frontierIds":["service-install-catalog-owner-concurrency-closure-main"]}}
